{
  "name": "Weather Alert - Scheduled Monitor",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## What this workflow does\n\nRuns every 6 hours, checks the temperature in Madrid,\nand if it's below 10°C it sends an alert to a webhook.\n\n**New concepts vs. the manual example:**\n- Schedule Trigger (time-based automation)\n- IF node (branching on data)\n- HTTP POST (sending data out instead of just GETting)",
        "width": 400,
        "height": 280
      },
      "id": "note-overview",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-260, -260]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "hours",
              "hoursInterval": 6
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "schedule-trigger",
      "name": "Every 6 Hours",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [0, 0]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "GET",
        "url": "=https://api.open-meteo.com/v1/forecast?latitude=40.4168&longitude=-3.7038&current=temperature_2m,wind_speed_10m&timezone=auto"
      },
      "id": "http-request",
      "name": "Fetch Madrid Weather",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [240, 0]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Same as before, but now we also expose `temperature` as a\n// plain number so the IF node can compare it.\nconst current = $input.item.json.current;\nconst units = $input.item.json.current_units;\n\nconst message = [\n  `Temperature: ${current.temperature_2m}${units.temperature_2m}`,\n  `Wind: ${current.wind_speed_10m}${units.wind_speed_10m}`,\n  `Updated: ${current.time}`,\n].join('\\n');\n\nreturn {\n  json: {\n    message,\n    temperature: current.temperature_2m,\n  },\n};"
      },
      "id": "code-format",
      "name": "Format + Extract Temp",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [480, 0]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "string": [],
          "number": [
            {
              "value1": "={{ $json.temperature }}",
              "operation": "lt",
              "value2": 10
            }
          ],
          "boolean": [],
          "dateTime": []
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "id": "if-cold",
      "name": "Is It Cold? (< 10°C)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.1,
      "position": [720, 0]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 1. Get your URL\n\nOpen https://webhook.site — it shows you a unique URL\nlike `https://webhook.site/abc-123...`.\n\n### 2. Paste it here\n\nReplace the url below with yours.\n\n### 3. Run & watch\n\nExecute the workflow, then check the webhook.site page —\nyour request arrives there instantly.\n\n> Tip: this is the same pattern you'd use with Slack\n> incoming webhooks or any API that accepts POSTs.",
        "width": 380,
        "height": 300
      },
      "id": "note-webhook",
      "name": "Webhook Setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [960, -300]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "https://webhook.site/REPLACE-ME",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "{\n  \"message\": \"={{ $json.message }}\",\n  \"temperature\": \"={{ $json.temperature }}\"\n}"
      },
      "id": "webhook-send",
      "name": "Send Cold Alert",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [960, 0]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "noop-warm",
      "name": "All Good",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.noOp",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [960, 200]
    }
  ],
  "connections": {
    "Every 6 Hours": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Fetch Madrid Weather",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Fetch Madrid Weather": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Format + Extract Temp",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Format + Extract Temp": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Is It Cold? (< 10°C)",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    "Is It Cold? (< 10°C)": {
      "main": [
        [
          {
            "node": "Send Cold Alert",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "node": "All Good",
            "type": "main",
            "index": 0
          }
        ]
      ]
    }
  },
  "settings": {
    "executionOrder": "v1"
  },
  "pinData": {}
}
